# The UI boundary's remote calls (P19 S3; scripts/febe_rpc_gen.py).
# One back-end function per line: called from the COP, it runs on the CPU.
# "direct: name" keeps a call direct (reviewed COP-safe: it reads only
# uncached words with one writer, or is built for both cores).
# ucop-fix (2026-10-26): the per-pass status reads, no round trip each:
#  audio_status: play_status and quiet_restart uncached (playback.c), no
#    recording status in the shell build (fe_be.c #error);
#  pcm_is_playing: pcm_playing is SHAREDBSS (pcm.c);
#  mixer_channel_status: the channel table is IRAM (uncached).
# ucop-fix2 (2026-10-26): mixer_set_tap is NOT COP-safe (the PCM lock
# masks only the caller's core's FIQ, its depth is a plain increment), so
# it crosses, and so do viz_tap_open/viz_tap_close (the hook, the clean
# and the free on the CPU, where the lock keeps the FIQ out of the tap);
# the DSP's and sound.c's setters cross too (the codec reads them on the
# CPU), the EQ's set as one call (ui_eq_dsp_set, audio_out.c).
# p19-bssfix (2026-10-26): functions only.  --wrap redirects every
# reference, so a listed data object made the shell read the stub's code
# (fat_slot_fault, ata_flush_stats, rbfs_rename_fault: the device log's
# opcode "counters"); their getters cross instead.  febe_link_check.py
# fails on a listed name that the linked firmware defines as data.
direct: audio_status
direct: pcm_is_playing
direct: mixer_channel_status
